I will implement the ChangeCalculator using a greedy algorithm (which works for canonical coin systems like the examples given) and handle edge cases: negative change throws an exception, and if the change is smaller than the smallest coin or cannot be made exactly, throw an exception. The constructor stores the coin list (assumed sorted or not? We'll sort descending to be safe). The computeMostEfficientChange returns the list of coins used.

Changes needed:
- Implement constructor to store currencyCoins (sorted descending for greedy).
- Implement computeMostEfficientChange: throw IllegalArgumentException for negative grandTotal; if grandTotal == 0 return empty list; if grandTotal < smallest coin or cannot be represented exactly, throw exception; otherwise greedily pick coins.
- Use only standard Java libraries.

ChangeCalculator.java
```
import java.util.List;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Collections;

class ChangeCalculator {
    private List<Integer> currencyCoins;

    ChangeCalculator(List<Integer> currencyCoins) {
        // Defensive copy and sort descending for greedy approach
        this.currencyCoins = new ArrayList<>(currencyCoins);
        Collections.sort(this.currencyCoins, Collections.reverseOrder());
    }

    List<Integer> computeMostEfficientChange(int grandTotal) {
        if (grandTotal < 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Cannot compute change for negative amount: " + grandTotal);
        }
        if (grandTotal == 0) {
            return new ArrayList<>();
        }
        if (currencyCoins.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("No coins available to make change.");
        }
        int smallestCoin = currencyCoins.get(currencyCoins.size() - 1);
        if (grandTotal < smallestCoin) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Change amount smaller than smallest coin value.");
        }

        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        int remaining = grandTotal;
        for (int coin : currencyCoins) {
            while (remaining >= coin) {
                result.add(coin);
                remaining -= coin;
            }
        }
        if (remaining != 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Cannot make exact change with given coins.");
        }
        return result;
    }
}
